Z||000004||Mark Matthews||12-07-2001||09:02 AM||||Hey all, thanks!  I'm liking this car more and more each minute... minus the fact that the guy must have been pumping up the tires just before I got there!  Went out this morning to play with her a bit before I went to work and my front right is flat... DOH!  I'll just get new tires, and maybe make a fullsize spare... we'll see.<P>Finally did the compression on all cylinders.  Can I have a round of 150's for everyone!!!  Maybe a 2-7 psi difference!  I think the owner paid very close attention to this car.  Still gotta figure out the ECM code 32, the tube looks good.  Could use a vavle cover gasket on the 'close' cover.  When you guys talk about the engine, how do you discribe front and back of the engine?  I get confused cuz it's in the back!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I noticed the hose to the washer bottle is off.  I found the hose for it but it doesn't reach, plus there's some little funnel thing on it.  Am I missing a piece?<P>So here's what style Fiero it is, with help from BAM-BAM:  87GT Fastback, T-top, wing delete, AC (I don't know what's standard, so I'll list what I can), PS, PW, PM, AM/FM Tape, Cruise, seats don't have a single stain or rip, Almost perfect carpet (missing left floormat - grey and black), med mat red / grey, honeycomb wheels, headlight go up and down, flat FR tire!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I feels it's a good car, just needs a good bath, paint job/clearcoat job, and an engine cleaning (how much for a pro job on the engine?)  I know why alot of you are putting in new stereos tho!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>As for the Jalapeno thing, I've already started taking off the panels.<P>(EDIT) - still working on my left's and right's!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mark Matthews (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||Mark Matthews||12-07-2001||09:08 AM||||JUST KIDDING!!!<P>If I do the Jalapeno thing, it probably won't be till summer.  Who know's by then I'll probably want to keep this one and get another one for the kit!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||12-07-2001||10:07 AM||||Good find!<BR>Before you replace the stereo, just buy some Pioneer TSA-4103 speakers for the dash. Will make all the difference in the world, for $100 max.<P>Please don't cut up a T-top GT to make a Jalapeno.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||14
